<EnglishInstitutionalPage
  title="Privacy Policy | Canapalandia"
  description="Canapalandia privacy notice covering browsing, contact forms, newsletters and waitlists, optional analytics, Canapalandia Lab and user rights."
  canonical="/en/privacy/"
  alternateIt="/privacy-policy/"
  eyebrow="Privacy"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  lead="This notice explains which personal data may be processed when you use canapalandia.com and for what purposes."
>
  <section>
    <h2>Data controller and contact details</h2>
    <p>The Canapalandia editorial project is managed by <strong>Luca Sanna</strong>. For privacy-related requests, email <a href="mailto:info@canapalandia.com">info@canapalandia.com</a> or use the <a href="/en/contact/">Contact page</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Technical browsing data</h2>
    <p>The infrastructure required to deliver the site may process technical data such as IP address, date and time of the request, requested URL, browser or device information and log data. These data may be necessary to deliver pages, maintain security and availability, and diagnose technical issues.</p>
    <p>The site is hosted through Vercel and may use network and CDN infrastructure required to distribute content.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Contact forms</h2>
    <p>The Contact and Collaborate with Canapalandia forms collect the data needed to handle requests, reports and editorial proposals and are technically managed through <strong>Resend</strong>. The data are used to receive and reply to the request and for any related follow-up.</p>
    <p>The legal basis depends on the nature of the request and may consist of taking steps requested by the user, managing a relationship with the user, or the legitimate interest in replying to communications and reports. Data are retained for as long as necessary to handle the request and any related obligations.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Newsletter</h2>
    <p>Newsletter subscription is voluntary and requires explicit consent. The system uses <strong>Buttondown</strong> and transmits the email address; for technical and anti-abuse purposes, the IP address associated with the subscription request may also be transmitted.</p>
    <p>You can withdraw consent through the unsubscribe link included in communications or by contacting us.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Demand tests and waitlists</h2>
    <p>When an interest test is active, such as <strong>Drop 001</strong> or an experimental <strong>Canapalandia Shop</strong> test, the waitlist is used only to measure demand for a concept that is not yet on sale and, if the project passes the planned gates, to communicate the outcome or possible launch. Joining the waitlist is not an order, does not involve payment and does not create any obligation to purchase.</p>
    <p>In addition to the email address and, for technical and anti-abuse purposes, the IP address, metadata may record the campaign, product preference, creative version shown and consent context. Fields may include <code>campaign</code>, <code>preference</code>, <code>creative_version</code> and <code>consent_context</code>. These data are used to compare, in aggregate, interest in different concepts, products, formats or tested price ranges.</p>
    <p>Subscriber creation through Buttondown uses <strong>double opt-in</strong> by default: a confirmation email is sent and the subscription becomes active only after the email address is confirmed. Canapalandia does not force this mechanism to be disabled in demand tests.</p>
    <p>Demand-test-specific metadata are retained for the time needed to measure the experiment and manage any communication of its outcome. Within <strong>6 months after the individual test closes</strong>, the data are reviewed and deleted or anonymised when no longer necessary, except for the minimum data that may need to be retained to document consent or withdrawal, comply with data-subject requests, or avoid sending messages to unsubscribed addresses.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Analytics and measurement</h2>
    <p>Canapalandia may use Google Analytics, Ahrefs Analytics, Vercel Web Analytics and Vercel Speed Insights to understand site usage and measure performance and content. These optional measurement tools are activated <strong>only after the user makes a positive choice</strong> in the privacy panel.</p>
    <p>If you reject analytics, the site remains usable and optional measurement tools are not loaded by Canapalandia's configuration. Your choice is stored locally on the device to avoid asking again on every page and is requested again periodically or when the configuration changes substantially.</p>
    <p>You can change your choice through <strong>Privacy preferences</strong> in the footer. For details, see the <a href="/en/cookies/">Cookie Policy</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Canapalandia Lab</h2>
    <p>In Canapalandia Lab, the PDF/TXT file or the text of a COA certificate is processed in the user's browser. The certificate content is not sent to Canapalandia's servers by the analysis feature, and the PDF report is generated on the device.</p>
    <p>The browser may download technical libraries from external CDNs that are needed for processing, but the certificate file is not uploaded to those services by the analysis feature.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Providers and transfers</h2>
    <p>Technical providers such as Vercel, Resend, Buttondown and, subject to consent for measurement, Google and Ahrefs may be involved in delivering site functions. Depending on the service and context, these parties may operate under their own privacy roles and terms.</p>
    <p><strong>Buttondown, LLC</strong> is established in the United States and processes data needed to manage subscriptions and waitlists. Buttondown's contractual documentation provides for a Data Processing Agreement and, where required for GDPR-covered transfers to the United States, the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs, controller-to-processor module).</p>
    <p>Some other providers may process data through infrastructure located outside the European Economic Area. Where applicable, processing must take place under the mechanisms and safeguards required by European law and the terms of the relevant provider.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Main legal bases</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>operation and security:</strong> technical necessity and legitimate interest in security and service delivery;</li>
      <li><strong>contact requests:</strong> handling the request and, where applicable, pre-contractual steps or legitimate interest in communication;</li>
      <li><strong>newsletter and waitlists:</strong> consent;</li>
      <li><strong>optional analytics:</strong> consent.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Where provided for by Regulation (EU) 2016/679, you may request access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing and data portability; object to certain processing; and withdraw consent already given without affecting the lawfulness of processing carried out before withdrawal.</p>
    <p>You may also lodge a complaint with the Italian Data Protection Authority (Garante per la protezione dei dati personali) if you believe that the processing of your personal data breaches applicable law.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Unnecessary data and updates</h2>
    <p>Avoid entering particularly sensitive information or data that are not necessary for your request in the forms. You do not need to provide health data or personal documents to use the site's ordinary editorial content.</p>
    <p class="institutional-note">This notice is updated when services, providers or processing methods change. Last substantial update: 6 September 2026.</p>
  </section>
</EnglishInstitutionalPage>
